§§ `The funeral director (new role: ss 42, 43)`

-- s 42(a): the funeral director, unless the body is placed with an institution for medical education or research (s 42(b)) or
-- a coroner found a suspected death established (s 43). Organ donation is not placing the body (baseline finding 11).
#ASSERT `Must I notify the Registrar of this death` `as the funeral director` `in WA` FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must I notify the Registrar of this death` `as the funeral director` `in WA` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must I notify the Registrar of this death` `as the funeral director` `in WA` FALSE TRUE EQUALS no

-- ASSUMEd inputs: reading any of them stops the evaluation, so a case that passes with them shows they were not read.
ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked Hospital` IS A Hospital
ASSUME `an unasked How the parents apply` IS A `How the parents apply`
ASSUME `an unasked Kind of death` IS A `Kind of death`
ASSUME `an unasked Offence` IS A Offence
ASSUME `an unasked Reason the other parent does not sign` IS A `Reason the other parent does not sign`
ASSUME `an unasked Registry service` IS A `Registry service`
ASSUME `an unasked What is done with the remains` IS A `What is done with the remains`
ASSUME `an unasked Where the person died` IS A `Where the person died`
ASSUME `an unasked Who applies` IS A `Who applies`
ASSUME `an unasked Who signed the statement` IS A `Who signed the statement`

§§ `Each question, asked for every role it is not about: does not arise, and nothing else is read`

